\description{
Splom traces generate scatter plot matrix visualizations. Each splom
`dimensions` items correspond to a generated axis. Values for each of
those dimensions are set in `dimensions[i].values`. Splom traces support
all `scattergl` marker style attributes. Specify `layout.grid` attributes
and/or layout x-axis and y-axis attributes for more control over the axis
positioning and style.
}
\details{
\code{go_splom()} creates a validated graph object (a named list).
\code{add_splom()} creates one and adds it to a figure.


Nested objects are given as named lists or with their constructors, which
are linked from the arguments below. Every property is checked against
the plotly.js schema when the object is created or modified (see
\code{\link{plotly_obj-modify}}). One-sided formulas (\code{~col}) are
evaluated in the data, and then checked, when the trace is added with
\code{add_<trace>()} or \code{add_trace()}.
}
